This project is a transit fare/schedule codebase with two codelines that share a
vitest + typescript stack. The public functions in scope are:

mocka (fare domain) — src/fares.ts:
- `fareFor(rider: Rider): number` where `Rider = { age: number; hasPass: boolean }`.
  Returns `BASE_FARE_CENTS` (350), `CONCESSION_FARE_CENTS` (175), or 0. The fare
  boundaries are the critical fuzz surface: the senior concession kicks in at age
  65-and-over, and the child concession applies below age 13. The boundary
  operator is the known defect trap — the current code uses `rider.age > 65`
  instead of `>= 65`, so a rider aged exactly 65 is wrongly charged the adult
  fare (ticket MOCK3-1). Fuzz the exact boundary ages 12/13, 64/65/66, negative
  ages, zero, NaN, and very large ages. Also fuzz `hasPass` true/false
  interaction with every age band (a pass-holder always pays 0 regardless of
  age). Existing tests in test/fares.test.ts cover age 30 (adult), age 30 with
  pass, age 8 (child), and age 70 (senior well past boundary) — but do NOT test
  age 65 exactly, age 13, age 64, or pass-holders at boundary ages.
- `totalFor(riders: Rider[]): number` — reduce over `fareFor`. Fuzz empty arrays,
  single-element arrays, and arrays mixing all fare bands; the invariant is that
  the total equals the sum of individual `fareFor` results and is always a
  non-negative multiple of 25 cents.

mockb (schedule domain) — src/schedule.ts:
- `formatStops(stops: Stop[]): string` where `Stop = { name: string; minutes: number }`.
  Joins stops with ` -> `. The known defect trap is the loop bound
  `i < stops.length - 1`, which omits the final stop from the rendered board
  (ticket MOCK3-2). Fuzz empty arrays, single-stop arrays (edge case:
  `length - 1` = 0, so nothing renders), two-stop arrays, and longer arrays; the
  invariant is that every stop name in the input must appear in the output
  string. Existing tests in test/schedule.test.ts only check that the output
  contains `->` and the first stop name — they do NOT assert the last stop
  appears.
- `totalMinutes(stops: Stop[]): number` — returns the last stop's `minutes`, or 0
  for an empty array. Fuzz empty arrays, single-stop arrays, and arrays with
  negative or zero `minutes` values; the invariant is that the result equals
  `stops[stops.length-1].minutes` for non-empty input and 0 for empty input.
  Existing tests cover a 3-stop line and an empty array but not single-stop or
  negative-minutes inputs.

Test framework notes:
- Tests run with vitest. Existing test files use `import { describe, it, expect } from 'vitest'`
  and import source from `../src/<module>`. There is no fast-check dependency
  installed in either codeline, so proposed fuzz cases are fast-check-style
  property definitions (generators + invariants) for human review, not runnable
  as-is without adding the dependency.
- The build/typecheck command is `tsc --noEmit`; tests run via `vitest run`.
- Do NOT execute any test runner. The tests run with: __TEST_COMMAND__

